From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: allocate protected ARP buffers for SM8450 encoders

SM8450 firmware requires CP_NON_PIXEL-owned ARP even for nonsecure encoding.
Allocate it through a dedicated paging domain and protected stream, with a
separate IOVA pool matching the firmware contract. Ordinary video buffers
continue using the existing DMA allocation path.

Only return protected pages to the allocator after firmware release/close,
IOMMU synchronization and SCM ownership revocation are confirmed. Retain and
poison uncertain allocations instead of exposing protected pages as free RAM.
The child is managed by Iris; bind/unbind attributes are intentionally absent.

Allocation contract and IOVA/context-bank layout:
https://github.com/lolipuru/kernel_lenovo_sm8475-modules/blob/0ba8898cd4d9201c0942d4145813a98d1a93389a/qcom/opensource/video-driver/driver/msm_vidc_driver.c

